  <sharedRules>
    <rule name="Artificial Helpers" id="4de0-9696-d9c5-ae7a" hidden="false">
      <comment>4de0-9696-d9c5-ae7a</comment>
      <description>The following rules apply to DRONE models:
- DRONE models are ignored for the purposes of determing a unit&apos;s Starting Strength, and whether or not it is at Half Strength.
- DRONE models is ignored for the purpose of Morale Tests.
- DRONE models are ignored for the purposes of determing a unit&apos;s toughness characteristic, if it also contains models without the DRONE keyword.
- DRONE models are considered to have the same abilities that the unit that are assigned has, regarding unit&apos;s deployment or stealth, if that unit also contains models without the DRONE keyword.
- In your Movement phase, unit assigned DRONE models can be separated as a separate unit.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Battlesuits" id="db3a-1899-3f1f-6c4f" hidden="false">
      <comment>db3a-1899-3f1f-6c4f</comment>
      <description>BATTLESUIT models in this unit can make attacks with ranged weapons even when their unit is within Engagement Range of enemy units, but they can only make such attacks against enemy units that they are within Engagement Range of. 
In such circumstances, these models can target an enemy unit even if other friendly units are within Engagement Range of the same enemy unit.

Note that if a BATTLESUIT model has more than one ranged weapon, you can still choose to target units that are not within Engagement Range of its unit, but it will only be able to make the attacks with that weapon if all enemy units within Engagement Range of its unit have been destroyed when you come to resolve these attacks. 
In addition, when a BATTLESUIT model shoots a Heavy weapon, subtract 1 from the hit rolls when resolving that weapon&apos;s attacks while any enemy units are within Engagement Range of that model&apos;s unit.

INFANTRY BATTLESUIT models can move and shoot Heavy Weapons without penalty to the hit rolls.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Docked Drones" id="a152-a484-b9ff-720b" hidden="false">
      <comment>a152-a484-b9ff-720b</comment>
      <description>If this model is docked with another model:
- Any weapons this model is equipped with are considered to be equipped to the model it is docked with instead.
- Attacks cannot be allocated to this model and it does not count as a model on the battlefield for any rules purposes.
- Mortal wounds must be allocated to the model that is docked with instead of being allocated to this model.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Limited Parameters" id="79c6-ebcf-01bc-fca2" hidden="false">
      <comment>79c6-ebcf-01bc-fca2</comment>
      <description>If this unit contains only DRONE models, this unit cannot perform actions, except for Searching for targets, and loses the Objective Secured ability if it has it, and cannot gain it through any means.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Mechanical endurance" id="e685-bcdd-87ed-8a00" hidden="false">
      <description>Models in units with this Rule reduce the incoming damage by 1, to a minimun of 1.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Redundant systems" id="21d1-6b7b-62b8-e32a" hidden="false">
      <description>Each time a model with this Rule would lose a wound, roll one D6: on a 6+ that wound is not lost.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Stable gun plattform" id="b590-59b8-4c60-10c7" hidden="false">
      <description>Models with this Rule can Advance and shoot Assault weapons without penalty, and shoot with Rapid fire and Heavy weapons substractin 1 from the hit roll.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Ion weapon profile" id="b526-7aa5-3163-94ef" hidden="false">
      <description>Before selecting targets, select between Standard or Overcharge weapon profiles to make attacks with.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
  <sharedSelectionEntries>
    <selectionEntry name=" Sept selection" id="0e73-a754-93fe-e10d" collective="false" hidden="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
      <constraints>
        <constraint id="a54e-7815-b2fc-ed5c" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="true" percentValue="false" scope="force" shared="true" type="min" value="1"/>
        <constraint id="ff1f-f65b-6cb6-bc95" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="true" percentValue="false" scope="force" shared="true" type="max" value="1"/>
      </constraints>
      <costs>
        <cost name="PL" typeId="e356-c769-5920-6e14" value="0"/>
        <cost name="CP" typeId="2d3b-b544-ad49-fb75" value="0"/>
        <cost name="Pts" typeId="points" value="0"/>
        <cost name="RP" typeId="ed03-25cc-2681-bdce" value="0"/>
      </costs>
      <infoGroups>
        <infoGroup name="Philosophies of War" id="cae2-cc5e-60a7-102c" hidden="false">
          <modifiers>
            <modifier field="hidden" type="set" value="false">
              <conditions>
                <condition childId="dd89-06e9-3ef5-7fe8" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="true" percentValue="false" scope="force" shared="true" type="atLeast" value="1"/>
              </conditions>
            </modifier>
          </modifiers>
          <profiles>
            <profile name="Mont&apos;ka" id="1d03-d571-b1ed-18f6" hidden="false" typeId="4c50-d86b-df5f-5fbf" typeName="Philosophies of War">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Effect" typeId="d64f-ec60-6651-12df">- Each time a T&apos;AU EMPIRE unit makes a ranged attack against an enemy unit that is within half the weapon’s range, make an additional attack with the weapon (Rapid Fire 1--&gt; Rapid Fire 1+1), if that weapon is Twin-Linked (includes Twin in it&apos;s name), make 2 additional attacks instead.
- T&apos;AU EMPIRE units of your army can re-roll Advance rolls and Charge rolls.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
            <profile name="Kauyon" id="19ff-2a87-51e4-041b" hidden="false" typeId="4c50-d86b-df5f-5fbf" typeName="Philosophies of War">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Effect" typeId="d64f-ec60-6651-12df">- T&apos;AU EMPIRE units of your army can Fall Back and shoot in the same turn, but when doing so, subtract 1 from the hit roll.
- Re-roll failed hit rolls for ranged attacks made by T&apos;AU EMPIRE units of your army which didn&apos;t move in the previous movement phase.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
          </profiles>
        </infoGroup>
        <infoGroup name="Markerlights" id="0f1d-64f0-f22f-8bd8" hidden="false">
          <profiles>
            <profile name="1" id="9720-eea6-df9a-933e" hidden="false" typeId="a6e0-92ef-5257-5e3b" typeName="Markerlights">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Effect" typeId="2d50-80fd-f2d5-64d1">You can re-roll hit rolls of 1 for T&apos;AU EMPIRE models attacking this unit.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
            <profile name="2" id="9e32-865c-4fd6-1fb0" hidden="false" typeId="a6e0-92ef-5257-5e3b" typeName="Markerlights">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Effect" typeId="2d50-80fd-f2d5-64d1">The target unit does not gain any bonus for being in cover against attacks made by T&apos;AU EMPIRE models.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
            <profile name="3" id="b250-4dff-c3cc-9705" hidden="false" typeId="a6e0-92ef-5257-5e3b" typeName="Markerlights">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Effect" typeId="2d50-80fd-f2d5-64d1">Destroyer and Seeker missiles can be fired at this unit even if it&apos;s not visible for the firing unit. Attacks made by T&apos;AU EMPIRE models ignore the Hit roll penalty due to Indirect fire Rule.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
            <profile name="4" id="e348-b050-3c31-0858" hidden="false" typeId="a6e0-92ef-5257-5e3b" typeName="Markerlights">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Effect" typeId="2d50-80fd-f2d5-64d1">The target unit can&apos;t use &quot;Look out, sir&quot; and &quot;Hard to hit&quot; against T&apos;AU EMPIRE models attacking this unit with ranged weapons. In addition, T&apos;AU EMPIRE models attacking this unit can ignore any or all Hit roll modifiers.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
            <profile name="5" id="874f-3405-0500-c66f" hidden="false" typeId="a6e0-92ef-5257-5e3b" typeName="Markerlights">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Effect" typeId="2d50-80fd-f2d5-64d1">Add 1 to Hit rolls for T&apos;AU EMPIRE models attacking this unit.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
            <profile name=" Markerlights" id="2a71-969a-ffe9-04d4" hidden="false" typeId="a6e0-92ef-5257-5e3b" typeName="Markerlights">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Effect" typeId="2d50-80fd-f2d5-64d1">If a INFANTRY model fires a markerlight, it cannot fire any other weapons in that phase. When a unit is hit by a markerlight, place a counter next to it for the remainder of the round. 
The table below describes the benefits T&apos;AU EMPIRE models have when shooting at a unit that has markerlight counters. All benefits are cumulative.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
          </profiles>
        </infoGroup>
      </infoGroups>
